{"AnonDBStore.CreateOrUpdateDevice enforces the device cap with a separate CountDevices query before the insert/update, so concurrent requests can both observe count < limit and insert new rows, exceeding the configured limit": 0.9203985333442688, "AnonDeviceService.tagDeviceUI writes the device ID into localCache before persisting to DB and does not clear it on error; after a first ErrDeviceLimitReached, subsequent requests for the same device ID hit the cache and skip DB enforcement, allowing anonymous auth to succeed for ~29 minutes": 0.8710254430770874}